00:22:30.620 --> 00:22:32.240
Hey, Everett

00:22:32.240 --> 00:22:36.290
What am I {like }in your world?

00:22:36.290 --> 00:22:39.000
Let me take a look

00:22:39.000 --> 00:22:40.380
Hey, Everett

00:22:40.380 --> 00:22:44.170
According to you, there are lots of different worlds

00:22:44.170 --> 00:22:47.170
I'm not sure I understand

00:22:48.430 --> 00:22:49.130
"Hi, Dandy"

00:22:50.340 --> 00:22:51.050
"Hello"

00:22:52.300 --> 00:22:53.140
"How are you doing?"

00:22:54.390 --> 00:22:56.140
Hey, Ph.D.

00:22:56.140 --> 00:22:59.980
Your alternate worlds will always overlap and never interfere

00:22:59.980 --> 00:23:02.730
That blows my mind

00:23:02.730 --> 00:23:08.320
Things get harder when they cool

00:23:08.320 --> 00:23:12.820
Things melt when they're heated

00:23:12.820 --> 00:23:15.120
This world is so full of rules,

00:23:15.120 --> 00:23:18.710
it's going to drive me crazy

00:23:18.710 --> 00:23:23.080
One dimension, two dimensions, three dimensions

00:23:23.080 --> 00:23:26.960
A supernova is spreading from west to east

00:23:26.960 --> 00:23:29.670
Easy game, easy game,

00:23:29.670 --> 00:23:31.220
too easy game

00:23:31.220 --> 00:23:35.680
The way there is fine, but what about coming back?

00:23:35.680 --> 00:23:40.600
A dream of a never-ending dream

00:23:41.640 --> 00:23:44.940
A wonderful, milky kiss

00:23:45.690 --> 00:23:52.030
Will this universe expand forever?

